  message: "Materialized in Phase-7 reconciliation (F94.A1). Consolidation 3a folded this as an EXTENSION of the MQ test-string event_publishes finding (WI-nitob, same false-positive CLASS), so it was not independently carded/judged; but the producers and fixes differ (database_query.py:430-478 matches table names repo-wide, no scoping, vs the MQ linker), making it RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT. Evidence: frozen substrate.json — all 17 references edges with meta.table_name link SQL-string literals in the linker's OWN test files to a 'users' table in an unrelated fixture, conf 0.85. INVALIDATION-RISK at discovery (synthetic 2-file repro=0) but substrate+source mechanism direct. Priority P1 by analogy to the FP-linker family (blind sev 4); NOT independently blind-judged. RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT to WI-nitob."  # daa5
- op: discuss  # bdaa
  at: '2026-06-27T00:21:28Z'  # bdaa
  by: agent  # bdaa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bdaa
  clock: 3  # bdaa
  nonce: bdaa  # bdaa
  message: "Test-sourced face DRAINED by linker-evidence-gating:F1 (PR #4317, dev af0b573ea1). The database-query linker now scans via the shared discovery.find_non_test_files gate instead of find_files, so SQL string literals in test files no longer synthesize call_site symbols or phantom table 'references' edges.\n\nEvidence: the filed repro was 17 references edges, ALL sourced from the linker's own test files. The gate excludes those test files at the scan chokepoint (594 of 922 candidate files now excluded repo-wide). Production-path test TestTestFileGating in test_database_query_linker.py asserts a SQL literal in a test_*-named file + a tests/-dir file emits zero symbols/edges, while the identical query in a production-named file still links (1 symbol, 1 references edge).\n\nKEPT OPEN (todo_hard) for the RESIDUAL named in the title — 'no file/package scoping': F1 only removes the test-sourced phantom refs; it does NOT add cross-package scoping for PRODUCTION queries. A production query referencing a same-named table declared in a different package could still produce a cross-package phantom reference (the global flat table lookup at database_query.py ~461-473 has no package scoping). This production face was never independently reproduced (the original 17 were 100% test-sourced; synthetic 2-file repro was 0), so it needs a fresh-substrate re-verification: if 0 production cross-package phantom refs remain, this can close; otherwise the scoping fix is a separate change (sibling of WI-timon's package-scoping work)."  # bdaa
